# sha2lato agent runtime config.
# Copy to secrets/.env.agent (gitignored) and fill in — or run:
#   ./deploy/configure.sh        (interactive; handles this file for you)
# This file is read by compose (env_file) and never committed with real values.

# ── Required ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Self-hosted Discord bot token — see docs/discord-bot.md.
# Headless: kimaki reads it on start and persists it to /data/kimaki.db,
# so later restarts work even without this variable.
KIMAKI_BOT_TOKEN=

# ── Optional ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Discord category name for this machine ("Kimaki <MACHINE_NAME>")
MACHINE_NAME=sha2lato

# Set to 1 to start every session in a fresh git worktree (kimaki --worktrees)
KIMAKI_WORKTREES=

# Optional model provider API keys — an alternative to /login in Discord.
# Only set what you use; OAuth subscriptions (Claude Pro/Max, ChatGPT) need
# nothing here, just run /login in Discord once.
# Voice messages + `kimaki tts`: set OPENAI_API_KEY or GEMINI_API_KEY (or use /transcription-key in Discord).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── Workflow pack (choose ONE: pack[@version]) ─────────────────────────────
# agents-opencode — agent roster (orchestrator, codebase, review, ...) + 16
#                   commands + 27 skills (all languages). Default.
# superpowers     — methodology plugin (brainstorm → plan → TDD).
# none            — plain OpenCode + baked skills only.
# No version = latest, re-resolved each container start. Pin exact versions
# to lock them (fetched once, then cached on the volume):
#   agents-opencode@3.1.2      superpowers@v7.0.0
AGENT_PACK=agents-opencode
# superpowers only: uncomment to allow the version-only telemetry ping
# SUPERPOWERS_DISABLE_TELEMETRY=0
# Note: when superpowers is active, leave KIMAKI_WORKTREES unset — it
# manages git worktrees itself.

# ── Extra skills (default on; set 0 to disable) ────────────────────────────
# ponytail — minimal-code discipline plugin (injects the ruleset every turn
#            + /ponytail commands). Works alongside any workflow pack above.
PONYTAIL=1
# Optional: override the pinned ponytail plugin spec
# PONYTAIL_SPEC=@dietrichgebert/ponytail@5.3.2
# graphify — repo → knowledge-graph guide for the agent (the graphify CLI is
#            baked into the image; this only controls the usage guide).
GRAPHIFY=1

# ── Optional: git identity & commit signing ────────────────────────────────
# Agent commits use a baked default identity ("sha2lato agent
# <agent@sha2lato.local>"). Override it here, or enable SSH commit signing
# with a dedicated key at secrets/ssh/signing_key (register its .pub:
# GitHub → Signing Key; Forgejo → account key, which also authenticates —
# see docs/secrets.md). Then:
# GIT_USER_NAME=
# GIT_USER_EMAIL=
# GIT_SIGN=1
